 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "Want to make a film just by asking? Let's install Script2Film."
  },
  {
   "text": "Two ways in. Live in the terminal? Clone the repo, start Claude Code, and say: follow docs/INSTALL.md. That's all."
  },
  {
   "text": "Everyone else, this one's for you: Claude Code Desktop."
  },
  {
   "text": "Download the Claude desktop app and sign in. The Code tab needs a paid plan."
  },
  {
   "text": "Good news: nothing else to install first. The app already includes Claude Code."
  },
  {
   "text": "Click Code at the top of the sidebar, pick Local, then Open folder, and choose an empty one."
  },
  {
   "text": "Now give it one request: clone Script2Film and follow docs/INSTALL.md."
  },
  {
   "text": "It runs in Auto mode, so it just keeps going. Want to approve each command yourself? Switch to Manual."
  },
  {
   "text": "It works through the steps: Python packages, the renderer, two fonts, and the voice model."
  },
  {
   "text": "The voice model is the slow part, about twenty minutes."
  },
  {
   "text": "Last, it runs the install check. Ready to go? You're set."
  },
  {
   "text": "On VideoExpress? Ask for shots in the same breath: make this script into a film, with VideoExpress shots."
  },
  {
   "text": "It writes the shot prompts, sends them, and cuts the clips into your film."
  },
  {
   "text": "Then just say: make examples/coffee into a film. See you next time!"
  }
 ],
